{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "PostShor",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/postshor/postshor",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "C-TLS-GROUPS",
              "name": "CTlsGroups",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "TLS group list set without a post-quantum hybrid group"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "TLS group list set without a post-quantum hybrid group. ECDH is broken by Shor's algorithm on a cryptographically relevant quantum computer. Data protected by this key exchange can be recorded now and decrypted later (harvest-now-decrypt-later). NIST IR 8547 (draft) deprecates it after 2030 and disallows it after 2035."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded. OpenSSL 3.5+ supports ML-KEM, ML-DSA and SLH-DSA and offers X25519MLKEM768 in TLS by default; liboqs for other algorithms.",
                "markdown": "**Fix:** Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded. OpenSSL 3.5+ supports ML-KEM, ML-DSA and SLH-DSA and offers X25519MLKEM768 in TLS by default; liboqs for other algorithms."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "cryptography",
                  "post-quantum",
                  "source"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "precision": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CFG-TLS-NO13",
              "name": "CfgTlsNo13",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "TLS 1.3 not enabled (post-quantum key exchange requires TLS 1.3)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "TLS 1.3 not enabled (post-quantum key exchange requires TLS 1.3). SSL 3.0 / TLS 1.0 / TLS 1.1 is already insecure today, independent of quantum computing."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Replace with TLS 1.3 (required for hybrid post-quantum key exchange).",
                "markdown": "**Fix:** Replace with TLS 1.3 (required for hybrid post-quantum key exchange)."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "cryptography",
                  "post-quantum",
                  "config"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CFG-NGINX-CURVES",
              "name": "CfgNginxCurves",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "nginx ssl_ecdh_curve excludes post-quantum hybrid groups"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "nginx ssl_ecdh_curve excludes post-quantum hybrid groups. ECDH is broken by Shor's algorithm on a cryptographically relevant quantum computer. Data protected by this key exchange can be recorded now and decrypted later (harvest-now-decrypt-later). NIST IR 8547 (draft) deprecates it after 2030 and disallows it after 2035."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded.",
                "markdown": "**Fix:** Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "cryptography",
                  "post-quantum",
                  "config"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CFG-SSH-KEX",
              "name": "CfgSshKex",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "SSH KexAlgorithms set without a post-quantum hybrid"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SSH KexAlgorithms set without a post-quantum hybrid. ECDH is broken by Shor's algorithm on a cryptographically relevant quantum computer. Data protected by this key exchange can be recorded now and decrypted later (harvest-now-decrypt-later). NIST IR 8547 (draft) deprecates it after 2030 and disallows it after 2035."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded.",
                "markdown": "**Fix:** Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "cryptography",
                  "post-quantum",
                  "config"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CS-RSA-ENC",
              "name": "CsRsaEnc",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RSA encryption (.NET)"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "RSA is broken by Shor's algorithm on a cryptographically relevant quantum computer. Anything encrypted this way can be recorded now and decrypted later (harvest-now-decrypt-later). NIST IR 8547 (draft) deprecates it after 2030 and disallows it after 2035."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition for encryption/key transport; ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204); SLH-DSA (FIPS 205) or LMS/XMSS for long-lived firmware/root keys for signatures. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded. .NET 10 adds MLKem, MLDsa and SlhDsa; Bouncy Castle .NET for earlier runtimes.",
                "markdown": "**Fix:** Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition for encryption/key transport; ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204); SLH-DSA (FIPS 205) or LMS/XMSS for long-lived firmware/root keys for signatures. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded. .NET 10 adds MLKem, MLDsa and SlhDsa; Bouncy Castle .NET for earlier runtimes."
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "cryptography",
                  "post-quantum",
                  "source"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.1",
                "precision": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CS-ECDH",
