              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "TLS CurvePreferences pins classical groups only, disabling Go's default hybrid PQ key exchange. ECDH is broken by Shor's algorithm on a cryptographically relevant quantum computer. Data protected by this key exchange can be recorded now and decrypted later (harvest-now-decrypt-later). NIST IR 8547 (draft) deprecates it after 2030 and disallows it after 2035."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded. Go 1.24+ ships crypto/mlkem and enables X25519MLKEM768 in crypto/tls by default.",
                "markdown": "**Fix:** Migrate to ML-KEM-768 (FIPS 203), deployed as the hybrid X25519MLKEM768 during the transition. Prioritise this: the exposure starts the day data is recorded. Go 1.24+ ships crypto/mlkem and enables X25519MLKEM768 in crypto/tls by default."
